      "function": "smtp_server_connection_data_chunk_init",
      "line": 541,
      "code": "data_cmd->chunk_first = (conn->state.data_chunks++ == 0);",
      "note": "First project-side state derived from the witness SMTP command stream: the first `BDAT` command marks chunking as active on the connection and tags this command as the first chunk, which later enables both the shared DATA-input alias and the `DATA`-after-`BDAT` bad-sequence path.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib-smtp/smtp-server-cmd-data.c",
      "function": "cmd_data_destroy",
      "line": null,
      "code": "if (data_cmd->chunk_last ||\n\t\t!smtp_server_command_replied_success(command)) {\n\t\t/* clean up */\n\t\ti_stream_destroy(&conn->state.data_input);",
      "note": "Local fix commit `9f5e723974420af0014a397bb390b57f3b9a9431` adds `data_cmd->main_input` in `cmd_data_start_input()` and guards this cleanup with `data_cmd->main_input == conn->state.data_input`, which is exactly the missing ownership check here. The staged `patch.diff` artifact is unrelated.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib-smtp/smtp-server-cmd-data.c",
      "function": "cmd_data_destroy",
